description:
Define the Hermes marketplace submission checklist that ag-infra-cdp (agentguides/infra) will execute. Research actual Hermes plugin catalog requirements (manifest fields in plugin.yaml, listing metadata, icon/description, license) and enumerate:
- pre-submission verification: clean install via `hermes plugins install`, enable, `hermes guide status`, uninstall via `hermes guide uninstall-self` + `hermes plugins remove` leaves no residue outside $GUIDE_HOME;
- listing target: default vs community listing (launch plan line 336 says aim for default/community inclusion);
- metadata + versioning requirements from the packaging scoping doc;
- post-submission: install-metrics tracking (launch plan line 342).

Acceptance criteria: checklist doc exists, every item is verifiable (command or artifact), and it distinguishes what this repo must provide vs what ag-infra-cdp executes.

Filed autonomously during overnight backlog-grooming session; pending human review.

Define the compat/verify story between the plugin and runtime version ranges. The shim install hook already runs `guide --version`; extend the design to:
- declare a supported runtime range (e.g. agentguides >=0.5,<0.6) in one canonical place (plugin.yaml or profile bootstrap);
- fail fast with operator-actionable messaging on out-of-range runtimes;
- a repeatable verification matrix (plugin version x runtime version x hermes version — note hermes 0.16.0 vs 0.17.0 differences recorded in runtime/.planning/research/hermes-acp-mcp-tools-blocked.md, including the missing `mcp` SDK in the pipx 0.16.0 install);
- where the matrix runs (local just target vs CI) — scoping only, implementation may be a follow-up.

Acceptance criteria: range declared and documented, failure behavior specified, matrix enumerated with a named execution mechanism.

Filed autonomously during overnight backlog-grooming session; pending human review.
